2122:# --- TASK-260720-1pvfj5 additions -------------------------------------------
2127:# §5.0 / F1. ONE operator input on a native host: the approved absolute GOROOT.
2128:# GO and GOFMT are DERIVED from it so a cross-root pairing cannot be expressed.
2129:# The empty default is what hosted GitHub runners use -- there actions/setup-go
2130:# owns PATH in a fresh image and the step sets TOOLCHAIN_ALLOW_PATH=1, which
2131:# relaxes the path SHAPE only; every identity assertion still runs.
2136:# Every Go invocation in this file runs under this prefix -- the environment is
2137:# SUPPLIED, not assumed, and require-toolchain reads both settings back.
2143:# macOS ships `shasum`; Linux ships `sha256sum`. Both print "<hash>  <path>"
2144:# and both accept -c, so every recipe below is portable across the two.
2153:# TASK-260729-2kaopg measured `go test ./...` exiting 1 at Go's 10-minute
2154:# default in cmd/curator, twice. 30m is that task's recorded recommendation.
2157:# The committed-pin conformance root. CI exports CURATOR_CONFORMANCE_ROOT on the
2158:# step, so PIN_ROOT inherits it there; locally the caller passes PIN_ROOT=...
2159:# Either way require-pin-root fails closed when it is empty or not a root.
2172:# §5.0 / F1. Seven assertions, every one a comparison. The whole recipe is ONE
2173:# shell so `goexe`, `gofmtexe` and `r` are shared across the checks that need
2174:# them. Executably validated against /bin/sh stubs in §7.4 (cases F,G,I-Q).
2175:#   1. the pinned version still matches go.mod
2176:#   2. on a native host: GOROOT_EXPECTED present and absolute, GO/GOFMT absolute
2177:#   3. exact `go version`
2178:#   4. reported GOROOT == GOROOT_EXPECTED, byte for byte (native)
2179:#   5. the launcher IS $GOROOT/bin/go and the formatter IS $GOROOT/bin/gofmt
2180:#   6. GOTOOLCHAIN reads back as `local`  -- no implicit toolchain download
2181:#   7. GOENV reads back as `off`          -- no per-user go env file in the loop
2182:# 6 and 7 are read-BACKS, not just exports: a shim/wrapper launcher can override
2183:# its caller's environment, and this host already runs bare `go` through one.
2233:# rc5-native-control-inventory-v1 covers macOS and Windows only. On every other
2234:# host internal/godriver fails closed before the worker starts, so Linux runs
2235:# every package except that one. The list is DERIVED at run time and never
2236:# hand-maintained: a new package is included automatically.
2238:# F2: discovery lives INSIDE the recipe, behind a status-checked assignment.
2239:# `LINUX_PKGS = $(shell $(GO) list ./... | grep -v …)` is exactly what this
2240:# replaces -- Make's $(shell) discards the exit status, so a `go list` that
2241:# printed 3 of 40 packages and then failed became a green 2-package test lane.
2242:# Reproduced with shell stubs in §7.4: that form exits 0, this one exits 2.
2258:# Two invariants, both executable, both fail closed.
2259:#  1. the excluded package still exists under the path the exclusion names
2260:#  2. the set of packages that import it has not grown a third member that
2261:#     might drive godriver.Build from a Linux test
2263:# F2: both probes materialize COMPLETE `go list` output in a status-checked
2264:# assignment before any filtering. Revision 3 piped `go list` straight into
2265:# `grep -q`, which can exit 0 the moment it sees the match -- before `go list`
2266:# reaches a later package and fails. That guard reported ok on a failing list.
2282:# Full candidate identity: manifest digest, whole-tree digest, file count, and
2283:# every file. All four inputs are required; any mismatch aborts. All three
2284:# identities are emitted before conformance-candidate runs a single case.
2285:# CANDIDATE_INVENTORY is the file written by §5.2 C2; its own SHA-256 IS the
